From: Hariharan Ramanathan <quic_hramanat@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: increase HTT PPDU stats user limit

HTT_PPDU_STATS_MAX_USERS includes a spare entry because the PPDU parser
and update loops stop at MAX_USERS - 1.  With the current value of 8,
firmware reports containing eight users are therefore rejected and emit
repeated warnings.

Use the limit of 37 from the Qualcomm ath11k and telemetry implementations.
This lets ath12k retain statistics for up to 36 users instead of rejecting
valid multi-user PPDU reports from QCN9274 firmware.

Signed-off-by: Sowjanya vardhineni <quic_svardhin@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Hariharan Ramanathan <quic_hramanat@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_htt.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_htt.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_htt.h
@@ -1279,7 +1279,7 @@ struct htt_ppdu_user_stats {
 	struct htt_ppdu_stats_usr_cmpltn_ack_ba_status ack_ba;
 };
 
-#define HTT_PPDU_STATS_MAX_USERS	8
+#define HTT_PPDU_STATS_MAX_USERS	37
 #define HTT_PPDU_DESC_MAX_DEPTH	16
 
 struct htt_ppdu_stats {
